/-!
# The general Wythoff coarsened family, and the two fan clauses (#180)

## The referent, stated before the code

The object this file constructs has a standard name and a located definition; it is not a project
coinage.  It is the **coarsening of the Coxeter fan of a Coxeter chamber by the standard parabolic
generated by the irrelevant simple reflections**, i.e. the fan of the *Wythoff construction*
(Coxeter 1935, *Wythoff's construction for uniform polytopes*), in the generality in which
Alexeev–Engel use it.

* V. Alexeev, P. Engel, A. Thompson, *Stable pair compactification of moduli of K3 surfaces of
  degree 2*, arXiv:1903.09742v3, §4D, **Definition 4.16** (p. 26), with **Proposition 4.17**
  (p. 26) and **Remark 4.19** (p. 27).
* The same construction in the paper this issue names,
  V. Alexeev and P. Engel, *Compactifications of moduli spaces of K3 surfaces with a nonsymplectic
  involution*, §9, `sec:semifan`, **Definition `def:generalized-cox-semifan`**, whose displayed
  formula is

  > Modulo `W`, the fan `𝔉_gen` has a unique maximal dimensional cone
  > `𝒞_gen = ∪_{w ∈ W_dirr} w.𝒞`, where `W_dirr = ⟨w_i | i ∈ V_irr⟩`.
  > All the other cones in `𝔉_gen` are the faces of `𝒞` and their `W`-translates.

  (Source text at `.tmp-sources/alexeev-engel-2el-coxeter-semifans.tex`, lines 350–357, from
  `dzackgarza/research` `writing/coble/papers/AE22/2el.tex` at research main `5edf0f6522`.)

So the referent is a **family of cones in one ambient space**, indexed by a Coxeter chamber `K`, the
active/irrelevant partition of its walls, and the two subgroups `W_irr ≤ W`:

* the **generalized chamber** (the maximal cone modulo `W`) is `𝒞_gen = ⋃_{h ∈ W_irr} h(K)`,
  the union of the `W_irr`-translates of the chamber;
* the **cones of the coarsened family** are *all faces of `𝒞_gen` and all their `W`-translates*
  (`Definition 4.16`, displayed formula).  AET's own paragraph following the definition of the
  relevant content of a vertex set `V'` makes the same identification: the cone `F'` of `𝔉_gen`
  defined by `V'` is the one defined by its relevant content, and `F' ∩ 𝒞` is the cone
  `F(relpart(V'))` of the reflection fan — i.e. the cones are the truncations of `𝒞_gen`, not the
  unreduced chamber faces.

Two source defects are recorded rather than copied, and both are filed in `COMPLAINTS.md` under
LC-05:

1. `Definition def:the-semifan` says "We define the semifan `𝔉(𝒯)` to be the generalized Coxeter
   fan for this set `V_irr` of **relevant** vertices", where its own preceding sentence declares
   `V_rel` the relevant set and everything else irrelevant.  That phrase contradicts the displayed
   definition, which quantifies over `W_dirr = ⟨w_i | i ∈ V_irr⟩`.  This file uses the displayed
   construction and the relevant/irrelevant partition, as the issue instructs; `W_irr` is the
   subgroup generated by the **irrelevant** simple reflections.
2. `Proposition 4.17(4)` says the cones are "`g(F)` for `g ∈ W` and the *relevant* faces `F` of
   `K`", i.e. the unreduced chamber faces.  This is **not** the same family as the cones of
   `Definition 4.16` once the rank is at least three: in `A₃` with `J = {a, b}` the relevant
   chamber face `F_{c} = K ∩ ker φ_c` is a proper sub-sector of the facet `𝒞_gen ∩ ker φ_c` of the
   generalized chamber (both are two-dimensional cones in the same plane, and
   `(-1, 5) ∈ 𝒞_gen ∩ ker φ_c` but `(-1, 5) ∉ F_c`), so `F_c` is not a face of `𝒞_gen`.  The
   landed `LeanCategories.Lattices.Valued.WythoffSemifan` builds the `4.17(4)` family, and this
   file builds the `4.16` one; the truncations `aetGeneralizedChamberFace φ W_J V` for active `V`
   are members of both (`truncation_mem` below), and the two families agree in rank two.

## What is constructed, and the two obligations

* `CoarsenedConeFamily M` — the **codomain**: a family of cones of the ambient space.
* `WythoffCoarseningDatum φ J` — the **domain**: the AET data (the chamber functionals, the
  active/irrelevant split, the two subgroups) together with *every AET hypothesis the construction
  uses* — `active_nonneg` (Proposition 4.17(1), the half that needs no finiteness of `W_irr`),
  `convex` (Proposition 4.17(1), "In particular, `L` is convex") and `irrelevant_flips`
  (the irrelevant reflection changes the sign of its own functional, which is what excludes the
  irrelevant faces).  Nothing assumes that `W_irr` is finite, that the maximal cone is finitely
  generated, or that the family is finite.
* `WythoffCoarseningDatum.coarsenedFamily` — **O1**, the general coarsened family, as the set of
  all faces of all `W`-translates of the maximal cone.
* `WythoffCoarseningDatum.coarsenedFamily_faceClosed` — **O2**, universal face closure: every face
  of every member of the family is a member.
* `WythoffCoarseningDatum.coarsenedFamily_inf_commonFace` — **O3**, universal pairwise
  intersection-as-common-face: the intersection of any two members is a face of each, hence
  (`coarsenedFamily_inf_mem`) again a member.

## The one general step that is not discharged here

O3 is proved from the statements `IsConeFace.inf_left_of_inter` / `IsConeFace.inf_right_of_inter`,
which are general facts about the set-level face relation, plus the single geometric input
`MaximalConesMeetInFaces`: **the intersection of two `W`-translates of the maximal cone is a face of
each**.  That input is the fan axiom for the *maximal* cones of the coarsening: it is the content of
AET Proposition 4.17(4) after the relevant content is reduced, and it is what makes the coarsened
cones glue into a (semi)fan — a semitoroidal compactification glues along its cones, so AE's use of
`𝔉(𝒯)` presumes it.  It is *not* proved here for the general datum, and it is not assumed as a
field of the datum either: it is a separate hypothesis of the O3 theorems, so that a reader sees
exactly what is missing.  It is discharged in the two cases the general construction reaches with
the material at hand: `maximalConesMeetInFaces_of_WJ_eq_top` (all walls irrelevant: then the family
has the single maximal cone `𝒞_gen` modulo `W`, and `𝒞_gen` is invariant under every linear
equivalence) and `maximalConesMeetInFaces_of_subsingleton` (trivial `W`).  The general case is filed
in `COMPLAINTS.md` (LC-11) with the searches run; what it needs is the chamber fan of the Tits cone,
i.e. that the translates of the fundamental chamber tile the Tits cone and meet along chamber faces,
which the repository has for `RootPairing` chambers and not in this functional generality.

## Scope

Nothing here claims the parent issue #24's remaining obligations.  There is no claim of
`W`-equivariance as a *property to be checked* (the family is defined as a union of `W`-orbits, so
equivariance is definitional and stating it would be a representation lemma, not a theorem),
no claim of local finiteness (false for infinite `W_irr`: the maximal cones are indexed by the
infinite group and a point of the interior of `𝒞_gen` lies in infinitely many of them — see
`WythoffInfiniteParabolicExample.mem_infinitelyMany_maximalCones`), no rationality or finite
generation claim (a maximal cone of an infinite parabolic is not finitely generated), no
specialization to finite `W_J`, and no toric realization.

